{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>For to a man.</b> There is a man who is good before Elohim, and He has not given him toil, but has given him wisdom and knowledge and joy in wealth after he toils in it, like the matter of Jachin, and a righteous man shall wear it. Or the explanation may be that his joy is his rejoicing in his portion, whether much or little." "<b>And to the sinner.</b> He has given him business to occupy himself with, to gather wealth, and in the end He gives it to the man who is good before Elohim. And so the one who occupies himself with gathering wealth turns out to be occupying himself with hevel and a striving of spirit."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:02.215926598Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}